<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Braganza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1442">1442</a>–<a href="/years/1910">1910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Braganza dynasty, Braganzas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Braganza was the royal dynasty of Portugal from 1640 to 1910 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 1822 to 1889. Descended from an illegitimate son of John I, the dukes of Braganza became the greatest nobles of Portugal, and in 1640 Duke John led the revolt against Spanish rule and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> IV. The family moved to Brazil in 1807–08, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Pedro I</a> became the first Emperor of Brazil. It lost the Portuguese throne in the revolution of 1910.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-braganza.jpg" alt="House of Braganza" width="300" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zulske heraldry · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duchy_of_Braganza_(1640-1910).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
